  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile (config_005/006) achieves ~0.65 acc, a large jump over singleprofile (0.52), and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) makes negligible difference. The key remaining uncertainty within the RNA-only space is whether the scgpt encoder can outperform scvi_n200 in this multiprofile regime. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable swap from config_005, isolating the encoder effect while holding profile setting and aggregation fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: the answer directly determines which RNA encoder to pair with image in all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 030-039 vs 042-051). Resolving encoder superiority before committing budget to multimodal runs avoids potentially running 8+ multimodal configs with a suboptimal encoder. It is the highest-leverage uncertainty to close given the limited budget."
